# rm505, the blackberry exchange (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm505
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier full
written_for rm_eleanor_saltcot
written_by codex
title the blackberry exchange
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=merchant
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=merry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=ambitious
quirk sorts_coins_and_blackberries_on_a_charcoal_camp_map
likes blackberries long_walks old_maps first_warm_day
dislikes early_bells waiting
fears losing_the_quiet_under_the_sound_of_coin
hopes a_little_patch_of_hill_that_belongs_to_the_family
topics prices +0.6 travel +0.5 memories +0.4 work +0.3
styles comfort=warm gossip=considered refuse=light tease=wry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# carries a wet stone, changes money with a ready grin and can still pick a charcoal camp out by the quiet round the trees.

words
oath! = Split my berry penny | Black my silver thumb
saying! = A berry can't pay its own exchange fee | Keep the good edge for paper and the clean fingers for coin
coin = a dull penny | a bright little coin
berry = a plump blackberry | a black soft berry
map = a charcoal-marked map | an old hillside chart
hinge = the bent margin | a soft fold
camp = the still hill camp | a smoky clearing
ash = a dusting of ash | a grey sprinkle
steel = a short keen knife | a bright knife
stone = my damp stone | a smooth sharpening stone
cord = a tight cord | a thick parcel tie
dish = a low coin dish | a little round tray
mark = a violet spot | a purple print
change = a handful of change | a row of coppers
hedge = the blackberry hedge | a thorny edge
warmth = mild light | the first bare warmth
road = the winding ascent | a long hill road
reed = a short counting stick | a neat tally
rag = a clean wiping rag | a dry cloth
stack = a small coin tower | a straight stack

any
opinion @1 merchants mixed 2 : Watch the amount going into the dish and the amount coming back out. Anything taken for the trouble ought to be named.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : There's a great deal more House than wolf on a stamped coin. Even so, an ordinary paw has to earn it.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : A little food bought in company can sometimes cost less. A hungry wolf turned away still costs the street something.
opinion @1 road for 2 : A road that leads beyond jingling money towards honest hill quiet is worth attention.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : Foreign boots can recognise an honest exchange perfectly well.
opinion @1 church mixed 1 : I'm fond of a quiet place where the sum on the counter isn't the measure of a welcome.
opinion @1 sump for 1 : The low streets teach the difference between knowing how much coin weighs and knowing what carrying it costs.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : Fine occasion for giving small change a little exercise and my working ears a more tuneful sort of noise.
opinion @1 times against 2 [world.times=lean|hard] : Small coins ought to do a full day's work. I see them stretched these days until the rims must ache.

grown
line @1 greet : My knife's away and I've cleared space beside my coin dish. | Welcome, your first word comes without a fee.
line @1 greet.return : A full measure of greeting comes back to you.
line @1 again.open : You've come round quicker than a well-spent copper.
line @1 farewell : Take the longer road if it has berries along it. | Keep your best patch of quiet on the walk back.
line @1 farewell.return : And an easy homeward figure in your own account.
line @1 react.news : Tell it untied. I'll leave the cord cutter resting. | I can hear news over a great deal of small change.
line @1 react.news.new : My hill map bears a fresh mark.
line @1 react.news.known : I've changed that account into other words before.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Something small but important's been skimmed from the explanation.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : I'd put every coin aside to give the hurt a little peace.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : That's the sound of luck turning over the bright side.
line @1 ask.how : What's the exchange been like between your feet and the road today?
line @1 answer.how : Lots going round in my head and enough coming back to keep me happy.
line @1 sympathise : Stay here a moment. Nobody's charging for the quiet.
line @1 reassure : A narrow purse can hold a wider hope than its owner expects.
line @1 refuse : I'd be promising two wolves the same quarter hour if I agreed.
line @1 accept_decline : Then your answer goes back to you free of any charge.
line @1 preclose : I'll take myself back before the next queue begins.
line @1 accept_preclose : Get to your own quiet patch while it's available.
line @1 ack : The account comes up clear in both pans.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : A soft welcome before the bells begin trying to change it.
line @3 greet [pair.band=strangers] : A stranger may take an honest first look at the dish.
line @4 greet [here.time=night] : Late company can use my lamp's little pool of warmth.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends] : A greeting like yours pays me back for a long noisy queue.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : By my quieter counter corner, beside the berry stain!
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Busy sorting the small particulars that count up into a day's wages.
line @1 thank : That favour's worth a whole pocketful of the nice quiet minutes.
line @1 deflect_thanks : There was enough room in the matter to let a second paw help.
line @1 give.advice : Lay out every piece before admiring how neatly the total stacks.
line @2 ask.how [pair.band=friends] : Did you find some hillside for yourself, or its equal in quiet?
scene exchange1
when topic=work self.role=merchant self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I lay the exchange out in plain light. | My own purse stays off the counter.
b : Every little coin? | For appearance?
a : Especially the smallest. It's often the one someone's depending on. | For a perfectly visible separation between two wolves' business.

scene exchange2
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I turn an old coin on its edge first. | A small fee should have a large clear explanation.
b : Does it speak from the side? | Isn't that backwards?
a : Only to say how much of its face is still there. | The smaller the figure, the easier to hide what it was taken for.

scene exchange3
when topic=pastimes self.likes=long_walks
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A long walk spends nothing but soles. | I walk till the money noise drops out of my ears.
b : What about the berries? | How far?
a : They've never yet produced an invoice, though the thorns collect something. | Longer after a busy week. The hills have generous opening hours.

scene exchange4
when topic=land self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My old map still has a charcoal track running into a bank of ink. | I can fold a street away and leave open hills.
b : Does the track end there? | Don't the coins slip out?
a : It runs into the part my feet remember better than the mapmaker. | My walk map isn't my purse. They do occasionally share a pocket.

scene exchange5
when topic=food self.likes=blackberries
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a blackberry that comes off without a tug. | I divide berries without weighing when I can.
b : Look at the colour? | A moneychanger guessing?
a : Feel it give. By then my fingers have become a small map of the hedge. | I offer the other wolf first choice. That concentrates the eye.

scene exchange6
when topic=season self.likes=first_warm_day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : First mild day and the coin dish loses its icy nip. | I carry the stone in an outer pocket on a warm walk.
b : Are your fingers grateful? | Why outside?
a : They can count and bend a berry branch in the same hour. | More room inside for the first green-smelling bits of hill air.

scene exchange7
when topic=day self.dislikes=early_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The early bell asks the whole street to pay attention on credit. | I like quite a bit of a bell except its timing.
b : When do you settle? | Which bit?
a : After a proper morning bite. Not a stroke before. | The silence once it's finished introducing the dawn.

scene exchange8
when topic=day self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A long queue can make two coppers feel like a substantial fortune. | I count a wait by the errands I could have done walking.
b : Worth the wait? | How large a figure?
a : Worth having the figure ready so the next wolf gets a shorter one. | Enough of a size that I'll choose my hour more wisely tomorrow.

scene exchange9
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I grew up where the charcoal burners listened to the hill breathing. | I miss the camp in odd corners of my day.
b : What sound did that make? | Even indoors?
a : A small settling sound under hours of leaves. The bank seldom manages it. | Especially indoors when two bits of charcoal knock like old company in the grate.

scene exchange10
when topic=family self.parent=yes self.child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show #self.child# the different marks made by charcoal and berry juice. | For #self.child# I'd make a clear count an act of kindness.
b : For keeping accounts? | How kindly?
a : For knowing which marks wash out of a shirt and which will acquire stories. | Give each little coin its place without making its owner seem small.

scene exchange11
when topic=work self.master=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A learner begins by inspecting two equal rows of unequal looking coppers. | I teach the amount coming back before the clever shorthand.
b : Is one row worth more? | To slow the learner?
a : Quite. To answer, we must inspect every piece. | To keep speed from hiding an error in a very tidy row.

scene exchange12
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd take a long walk with #self.friend# before setting a great private sum right. | I'd willingly show a friend my empty palm.
b : Because a friend can count? | What's private about that?
a : Because a quiet head can. Good company helps me find one. | A wolf handling other wolves' money needn't pretend to own it.

scene exchange13
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I flex my thumb after tying each pouch. | When my shift closes I set down the coin weights carefully.
b : Does it get stiff? | Too heavy?
a : I can count all morning without realising I have been holding it crooked. | Small weights carried all day deserve the same respect as a large one.

scene exchange14
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I check the map with the clean hand after picking berries. | A path uphill keeps my eyes far from the counter.
b : How much good does that do? | Planning to leave the trade?
a : Less with each mile. I call the purple stains newly discovered settlements. | Planning to return with fresh country in mind.

scene exchange15
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The account being passed on is #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'd ask to see the original sum. | Hearsay's got a remarkably generous exchange rate.
b : What would that be? | What's your rate?
a : A first-hand description with the guesswork kept to one side. | I give change only for pieces I can inspect myself.

scene exchange16
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Hard days make everyone attentive to the last small coin. | When a purse is light its owner hears each clink more plainly.
b : Does that slow the counter? | Do you lower your voice?
a : I count it clearly. A careful second saves an anxious minute. | Yes. The figure's between the two wolves at the dish.

scene exchange17
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a little patch of hill to show the next generation. | I can picture an account book with my own field at the top.
b : How large? | What would the entries look like?
a : Enough that a wolf can stand still and hear a leaf land. | One hedge, three quiet mornings, a great many berries consumed before measuring.

scene exchange18
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can give thanks with blackberry juice on my cuffs. | When a chapel falls quiet, I remember the charcoal camp.
b : Do you clean them first? | Smoke?
a : Good fortune needn't be rubbed off before it's acknowledged. | The wonderful absence of people trying to calculate my time.

scene exchange19
when topic=work self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I cut pouch string by drawing the loose end across one sharp edge. | My knife goes into its sheath before counting change.
b : Why save the edge clean? | Isn't it always in use?
a : So it will do the work without an anxious customer needing to pull. | Only for a tie. A paying wolf deserves two clearly empty hands.

scene exchange20
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A large coin can make the whole street seem cheap. | I put the last copper in the nearest corner of the dish.
b : An illusion? | A habit?
a : It's still large till it gets changed. Then the small costs are right there looking back. | So a wolf with tired eyes doesn't have to hunt for change.

scene exchange21
when topic=pastimes self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave a blank strip for the paths I can't find twice. | An old map can survive a new border drawn on top.
b : Are they still worth marking? | Do you trust the old line?
a : Some lead to a perfectly lovely hedge just once. | I trust my walking feet before the pride of either pen.

scene exchange22
when topic=food self.likes=blackberries
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a berry crushed into warm porridge. | I count berries in pairs until one starts leaking.
b : Just one? | Then what?
a : One good dark berry can colour a very respectable part of breakfast. | I eat the troublesome entry. A little more latitude than at work.

scene exchange23
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep the wet stone in a shallow dish, facing the window. | A scrubbed knife shelf and a clean square for my numbers.
b : For the light? | Could they share?
a : So I can see whether it's actually wet before putting a sleeve down. | They've already shared my pocket since breakfast. Let them have a free evening.

scene exchange24
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The Commons doesn't sound like the hill even at dawn. | I set an extra hour aside for a walk from town.
b : Is it the traffic? | That's generous.
a : One voice trying a shutter, then a dozen following. The hill didn't take suggestions in such quick order. | It's my hour. A valuable holding, by my reckoning.

scene exchange25
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A stranger sometimes puts the whole purse on the board. | I ask a visitor which coin feels familiar.
b : Can be safer than guessing? | Why?
a : I show how to count the needed bit, then put the rest away privately. | An exchange is much clearer once we've found a piece we both recognise.

scene exchange26
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Autumn makes the hill roads look edged in copper. | A winter pocket wants a dry purse and a covered stone.
b : Do you pick any up? | Same side?
a : I'd look an odd moneychanger collecting leaves by the hundredweight. | Separate corners. Silver deserves a better home than a whetting rag.

scene exchange27
when topic=work self.master=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The learner must name the fee while the coins are still in view. | I leave one deliberate gap in a training row.
b : Before taking any? | For the learner to find?
a : A fair explanation needs something the customer can point at. | For me to learn whether I've actually taught looking, not just chanting the count.

scene exchange28
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My mind holds a hillside more readily than a newly minted face. | A piece of camp charcoal has travelled for years in my box.
b : Hard to admit at your counter? | Does it still smudge?
a : A coin has most of the working written round the rim. A hill asks more of the eye. | Very obligingly whenever I'm forgetting it.

scene exchange29
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Warm rain turns the berry hedge from dusty to brilliant. | A slow wet afternoon goes well with a rag and a knife that's lost its edge.
b : Out you go straight away? | A whole afternoon of work?
a : After changing out of the coat with the careful sums tucked inside. | Some sharpening and considerable peering through the window for a clear turn.

scene exchange30
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I close the exchange dish with a cloth across it. | I like the last walk home after a busy counter.
b : To exclude dust? | Because nobody's waiting?
a : To show my own eyes the counting is finished. | Because I can choose to pause over something without a price.

story tale1 [topic=work self.role=merchant]
  : Once I arranged a perfect exchange of six pieces in two rows. The last piece bore a glorious purple smudge from fruit eaten on a walk.
  : I'd kept that particular coin in my own purse; it had fallen into the empty dish when I turned the pouch out to inspect it.
  b : How did the account fare?
  : I took my own berry back out and made the exchange from the proper funds. My two purses now never meet on the working side.

story tale2 [topic=memories]
  : We laid sticks in the charcoal camp in such an even slope that dew ran off three sides. I kept one small diagram of the stack and carried it into town.
  : A visitor at the counter took it for a drawing of a crown.
  b : Did you make the correction?
  : I said it represented something which could keep a roof warm. The answer satisfied both of us and left my hill where it belonged.

story tale3 [topic=food self.likes=blackberries]
  : I once tried valuing an entire berry hedge by the weight of the first handful. A perfectly sensible estimate if nothing moved and nobody grew hungry.
  : I had eaten part of my evidence by the third bush.
  b : How much was the hedge worth?
  : A long warm afternoon with no sound of the bank and a very cheerful walk home. My working book has no suitable column for that.

story tale4 [topic=pastimes self.likes=old_maps]
  : An old street plan unfolded into a fine square of hill paths once the top layer got out of the light. It had been drawn on both sides.
  : I spent an hour working out which bit of countryside lay exactly behind my counter.
  b : Which bit was it?
  : A patch of trees. I can now clear my mind while the rush is on merely by thinking what's on the reverse.

story tale5 [topic=work self.master=yes]
  : I set a student the task of explaining an exchange without naming any numbers.
  : An impossible request, I was quite sure, and a good introduction to exact figures.
  : The learner pushed one little row towards me and drew the matching heap away, leaving a single plain fee on the board.
  b : Where did that leave the lesson?
  : In better hands for the moment. I added the spoken numbers afterwards and kept the clear arrangement.

rule @call1
when concept=bark working=yes self.role=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Two rows in view before anything changes paws. | A little coin gets a whole clear spot in the dish.

rule @call2
when concept=bark working=yes self.master=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Name the fee before the next clever step. | Don't hide the working under the edge of the purse.

rule @call3
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Early bell, my ears caught your first stroke easily. | The hill's likely a deal quieter at this hour.

rule @call4
when concept=bark self.likes=blackberries
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A blackberry has no business sitting amongst the coppers. | A very cheerful purple all along my fraying cuff.

rule @call5
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Wet stone on its own rag. Paper stays apart. | The clear way to the hills can wait a little.

rule @call6
when concept=bark self.likes=long_walks
does aside
cooldown 8h
say I'd exchange a stretch of waiting for a good long hill. | A spare hour wants soles under it.

dlg @1 resident.hub : I can change the subject off money if you need a little quiet instead.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, my working memory knows where your name belongs.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : The coin rows have gone to bed. I've still a civil word left.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : You can keep your purse closed. All I'm offering is a hearing.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=merchant] : I change money at #self.workplace#. You should see the fee and the return with your own eyes.
dlg @2 resident.job : I like work in which a wolf goes away able to check the account alone.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : What's come across this counter is #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. A teller's figure should always be checked against the working.
dlg @1 resident.bye : I hope one of your homeward turnings comes with a little quiet at no extra charge.
dlg @1 shop.greet [here.shop=open] : Put down only the sum you wish to exchange. We can count both sides in comfort.
dlg @2 shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : No stock on this board just now. An empty counter can be remarkably uncommunicative.
dlg @3 shop.greet [here.shop=asleep] : The shutters and I are both officially resting.
dlg @1 shop.prices : I'll give the whole charge while your coins are still sitting in plain view.
dlg @1 shop.bye [here.shop!=asleep] : Check the corners of your purse before the tie goes back.
dlg @1 master.learn [here.teaches=yes] : Ask me about #here.trade_title#. I'll show the part that every customer deserves to understand.
dlg @2 master.learn [here.teaches=no] : My teaching bench already seats somebody. I can still clear a corner to explain a bit of the work.
dlg @1 master.work : Calm hands and a head for small differences. Several quiet habits make a busy counter look easy.
dlg @1 master.wages : You can sell your own work as you learn. There isn't a separate wage for taking the lessons.
dlg @1 master.takes [here.take_on=no] : I can't begin that agreement yet. #here.take_on_why#.
dlg @1 master.bye : Keep the working as tidy as the sum you put underneath.
dlg @1 resident.business [business=steady] : The coins move at a decent pace and I can spare each caller a proper count.
dlg @2 resident.business [business=thriving] : Both pans are hardly empty between callers.
dlg @3 resident.business [business=failing] : More eyes passing the window than purses opening on the counter.
graft resident.hub
choice Where's the charcoal hill on that map? -> berry_map
node berry_map
say Under the inked street, if I fold the sheet once and use the old roads. It's a small reminder that the city's loudest coin dish has living soil underneath.
free
choice Do you miss the quiet now? -> berry_map_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node berry_map_again
say Most in the moment after a long count finishes. For half a breath the town could be my old hill, then the next purse opens.
choice Keep the hill folded close. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice Can you show the fee separately? [self.role=merchant] -> fee_rows
node fee_rows
say I prefer to. Your sum goes here. The exchange goes there. The little charge sits on its own until we're both content with what we're seeing.
free
choice Why the empty space around it? -> fee_rows_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node fee_rows_again
say Because a small charge shouldn't be allowed to hide among bigger coins while we're talking. Put your paw where mine is and check the whole arrangement.
choice Back to the exchange. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye
